# graphify scan excludes — keeps the knowledge graph pointed at this project.
#
# .agents/ is the installed AI-skill library (34 skills + their reference checklists).
# It is ~92 markdown files of third-party process prose: left in the corpus it becomes
# the largest community structure in the graph and every doc in it needs a semantic
# extraction pass (LLM tokens) to describe instructions that have nothing to do with
# the storefront. graphify's own SKILL.md/references are still read by the agent that
# runs it, so excluding them from the *map* costs nothing.
#
# The logo/image entries are brand assets, not knowledge: each image forces its own
# extraction chunk (vision can't be batched), so two PNGs would cost two subagents to
# produce a node reading "a raccoon emblem".
.agents/
Logo/
*.png
*.ico

# Already skipped via .gitignore (detect honors it by default), listed for clarity in
# case someone runs `graphify --no-gitignore`.
.claude/
.qoder/
graphify-out/
